{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CRITICAL HANDOFF NOTE -- worktree venv fault (my setup error). I symlinked /Users/joeoakhart/jw-<id>/.venv -> janitor-2026-08-06/.venv. That venv is an EDITABLE install of janitor-2026-08-06/src, so 'import rebar' inside a jw-* worktree resolves to the OTHER checkout's source: pytest there did not exercise the worktree's own edits. Path-relative gates (make lint, mypy src/rebar) were fine; pytest results were not.\n\n- jw-2d1c: the agent detected this itself and replaced the symlink with a real venv (python3 -m venv .venv && make install), so its 723-passed run IS valid. It noted make install chained to make hooks and the Change-Id stamper was preserved (idempotent path).\n- jw-c9c6 and jw-da31: STILL SYMLINKED. Their reported pytest results are UNVERIFIED and must be re-run after 'python3 -m venv .venv && make install' in each worktree before anything is committed.\n\nSubagent outcomes (all uncommitted, awaiting my held-out validation):\n- 2d1c: forwards source into CodeReviewRequest, maps ref onto head (reviewed_head = ref or head), adds gate_source.copy_provenance + PROVENANCE_KEYS, annotates all three return points in _run_code_review_gate. Deliberately did NOT re-resolve the handle in the shim (a second resolve could pin a different SHA than the review actually read) -- good trust-boundary reasoning. Attempt count 1.\n- c9c6: answer (b), param removed. Attempt count 1. NEEDS RE-VALIDATION (venv).\n- da31: still running at handoff. NEEDS RE-VALIDATION (venv)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786076624728902001,"uuid":"2c540553-3ee6-4758-8e83-0de47a9b1f6e"}